WEBVTT

00:03.211 --> 00:06.381
Now commencing
the 57th Exterior Scouting Mission!

00:07.841 --> 00:09.384
Move out!

00:14.180 --> 00:15.932
We believe that the basement
of Eren Jaeger's home

00:16.016 --> 00:17.475
in Shiganshina District

00:17.976 --> 00:20.562
houses a secret of the Titans
that not even he is aware of.

00:21.980 --> 00:23.606
We are to head there.

00:24.941 --> 00:26.651
You rookies will be here,

00:27.027 --> 00:30.572
between the cart guard team
and the scout support team.

00:30.947 --> 00:34.117
Here, you will run alongside spare horses
and relay signals.

00:34.617 --> 00:37.162
Our Special Operations Squad
will be positioned here,

00:37.704 --> 00:39.372
on standby at the rear of the center rank.

00:39.789 --> 00:41.833
This is the safest position
in the formation.

00:42.500 --> 00:45.545
Not even the supply wagons
get this level of treatment.

00:57.766 --> 00:58.767
This isn't an Abnormal.

00:58.975 --> 01:00.643
- Cis!
- It has intelligence!

01:01.311 --> 01:04.064
It's just like the Armored Titan,
the Colossal Titan, and Eren!

01:04.814 --> 01:07.025
It's a human clad in a Titan body!

01:10.153 --> 01:12.530
This one is way more athletic
than the other ones!

01:12.864 --> 01:14.699
Damn! We were...

01:14.783 --> 01:16.326
We were too naive!

01:18.661 --> 01:20.121
She's protecting her nape?

01:20.455 --> 01:22.373
Damn it! There's no escape now!

01:22.457 --> 01:23.374
Jean!

01:23.458 --> 01:26.044
Avenge that suicidal maniac!

01:27.796 --> 01:29.214
She stopped?

01:29.923 --> 01:32.425
It was her! She killed him!

01:32.675 --> 01:35.512
That maniac finally got himself killed
as part of the right wing!

01:35.595 --> 01:37.806
She killed him!

01:52.821 --> 01:54.948
I'd say we bought enough time!

01:55.240 --> 01:56.866
Now let's get away from her, quick!

01:57.450 --> 01:58.368
What?

01:58.660 --> 01:59.744
Oh, no.

01:59.911 --> 02:00.745
Why?

02:01.246 --> 02:04.249
Is she heading for Eren?

03:49.354 --> 03:51.981
How is your omnidirectional
mobility gear, Armin?

03:53.066 --> 03:54.025
It's all right.

03:54.234 --> 03:57.654
It unclasped properly,
so it doesn't seem to be broken.

03:58.321 --> 04:00.490
I see. That's good to hear.

04:01.074 --> 04:04.619
But now what? We only have one horse.

04:05.995 --> 04:09.207
If Jean's horse comes back, all three
of us can get moving again, but...

04:10.625 --> 04:12.293
Damn it! What's the deal?

04:12.919 --> 04:17.632
Reiner's horse came back. Why won't mine?

04:21.469 --> 04:25.139
And we can't afford
to stay here any longer.

04:27.308 --> 04:30.478
Worst case scenario,
we'll have to leave someone here.

04:31.104 --> 04:34.065
How will we choose
who that someone should be?

04:34.941 --> 04:36.317
Armin, because he's hurt?

04:37.402 --> 04:40.029
Reiner, because he's big
and would be hard to ride with?

04:41.155 --> 04:44.492
Or should I go look for my horse on foot?

04:46.995 --> 04:47.912
Damn it!

04:47.996 --> 04:51.082
It's screwed up
that we even have to consider that!

04:51.457 --> 04:53.960
The three of us just managed
to escape death!

04:54.168 --> 04:56.462
This is one hell of a raw deal!

05:13.479 --> 05:14.439
Armin.

05:16.274 --> 05:17.150
Hey, Armin!

05:18.985 --> 05:21.237
I take it you're still a bit mixed-up?

05:21.821 --> 05:22.780
Yes.

05:23.156 --> 05:24.991
I'm still a little dazed.

05:25.366 --> 05:26.242
I see.

05:26.743 --> 05:28.786
Still, we need to decide now.

05:29.245 --> 05:30.663
It's a difficult choice,

05:31.122 --> 05:33.207
but it looks like one of us
has to stay behind.

05:36.461 --> 05:37.295
Wait!

05:38.337 --> 05:40.339
Let's fire a smoke signal first.

05:40.798 --> 05:42.508
If the formation kept moving forward,

05:42.800 --> 05:45.595
Row 4, Squad 3 should be nearby now.

05:51.392 --> 05:53.519
That was an emergency smoke signal.

05:54.020 --> 05:56.898
I doubt it's enough
to get our point across though.

05:57.607 --> 05:59.901
Armin, we'll only wait for three minutes.

06:00.401 --> 06:01.360
By then,

06:01.444 --> 06:03.654
- we need to choose who'll stay--
- I'll stay.

06:05.031 --> 06:09.410
But in exchange,
I need you to report something.

06:10.161 --> 06:12.121
Only to Commander Erwin, if possible.

06:12.205 --> 06:13.414
No, wait. Armin.

06:13.998 --> 06:16.000
You can report it yourself.

06:16.793 --> 06:18.461
Someone is coming!

06:18.836 --> 06:21.089
And they've brought two horses!

06:23.674 --> 06:24.967
That's...

06:27.678 --> 06:28.679
Christa!

06:29.472 --> 06:31.474
Guys! Are you okay?

06:34.602 --> 06:35.436
What?

06:35.520 --> 06:37.021
Hey, that's my horse!

06:37.897 --> 06:40.441
Whoa, there. Calm down, Buchwald!

06:41.067 --> 06:44.320
He came racing my way.
Something must have really spooked him.

06:45.363 --> 06:46.531
Did you guys fight a Titan?

06:47.490 --> 06:48.449
Armin!

06:48.908 --> 06:49.909
You're hurt!

06:50.243 --> 06:51.285
Are you all right?

06:51.494 --> 06:52.870
Yes, more or less.

06:54.622 --> 06:57.250
I'm impressed you willingly came here
after seeing that smoke signal.

06:58.042 --> 06:59.502
I happened to be nearby.

06:59.752 --> 07:01.170
Plus, I had found Jean's horse.

07:01.629 --> 07:03.589
You have a way with horses.

07:03.756 --> 07:05.633
Not to mention,
a remarkable sense of virtue.

07:06.259 --> 07:07.301
We owe you one.

07:08.719 --> 07:10.012
I'm just glad.

07:11.055 --> 07:16.352
I'm very glad that
the worst didn't happen to you guys.

07:22.066 --> 07:23.151
She's a goddess.

07:23.276 --> 07:24.402
A goddess.

07:25.445 --> 07:26.612
I want to marry her.

07:27.864 --> 07:30.408
Well, we better hurry back into formation!

07:30.491 --> 07:31.451
Oh, yes!

07:31.534 --> 07:33.244
There should be orders to retreat soon!

07:36.414 --> 07:40.334
Still, turning back not even an hour
after leaving the wall?

07:40.585 --> 07:43.004
Things look way grimmer than I thought.

07:43.463 --> 07:47.842
Plus, she's headed away from
the lead command squad for some reason.

07:48.217 --> 07:49.093
She?

07:52.096 --> 07:53.556
Green smoke signals?

07:54.182 --> 07:57.935
It sounds like the plan is to change
the route and continue the operation.

07:58.478 --> 07:59.437
Oh, no!

07:59.520 --> 08:00.897
They are not ordering us to retreat?

08:01.230 --> 08:03.858
What the hell is Commander Erwin thinking?

08:04.150 --> 08:09.447
All soldiers have the authority to decide
if the operation can't continue.

08:10.364 --> 08:13.117
Have the signals not reached
the command squad?

08:13.367 --> 08:16.829
Whether or not they know,
we only have one option in this situation.

08:17.455 --> 08:19.457
Defer to their judgment.

08:26.214 --> 08:28.424
Smoke signals. Green.

08:29.383 --> 08:31.093
Oruo. You fire it.

08:31.385 --> 08:32.386
Understood, sir!

08:33.387 --> 08:36.015
It feels like we're making
smooth progress right now.

08:37.642 --> 08:40.478
But I wonder how things actually are.

08:41.145 --> 08:43.940
I wonder if people have already died
on the front line.

08:44.190 --> 08:45.191
Reporting, sir!

08:46.108 --> 08:47.193
It's an oral message!

08:47.527 --> 08:49.695
Right wing Scouts, decimated!

08:50.196 --> 08:51.906
Detection network, partially out!

08:52.031 --> 08:54.534
Please pass this message on to the left!

08:55.660 --> 08:56.994
You heard him, Petra.

08:57.495 --> 08:58.371
Go.

08:58.454 --> 08:59.288
Yes, sir!

09:01.290 --> 09:02.416
The right wing?

09:03.292 --> 09:05.211
Isn't that where Armin is?

09:05.836 --> 09:10.758
Still, he and the others
are positioned closer to the center.

09:11.175 --> 09:13.427
The Titans couldn't have advanced
that far in.

09:15.471 --> 09:16.639
Black signals?

09:17.265 --> 09:18.391
An Abnormal?

09:18.766 --> 09:20.601
Eren. You fire it.

09:20.893 --> 09:22.103
Yes, sir!

09:22.520 --> 09:24.230
This is disgraceful.

09:24.897 --> 09:27.942
We've let them get pretty deep
inside the formation.

09:30.278 --> 09:32.697
Just over there is a Titan.

09:33.573 --> 09:36.200
Below that black smoke,

09:36.617 --> 09:37.994
someone is fighting?

09:50.798 --> 09:51.799
Damn!

09:52.091 --> 09:56.429
Look down here, you monster!

10:00.558 --> 10:01.601
Now!

10:10.109 --> 10:11.652
Three spots at once!

10:11.819 --> 10:15.489
She seems pretty smart,
but she can't defend against all of them!

10:16.073 --> 10:20.703
Cut her spine, ligaments,
or anywhere else that can stop her!

10:21.287 --> 10:22.705
Attack!

10:24.123 --> 10:26.167
So many are dead because of you!

10:26.250 --> 10:28.002
We're going to torture you to death!

10:34.592 --> 10:35.551
She jumped?

10:49.482 --> 10:51.525
Let go!

11:20.846 --> 11:22.181
Reporting takes priority!

11:22.348 --> 11:26.310
I have to let them know about that one!

11:33.984 --> 11:34.985
An Abnormal?

11:35.486 --> 11:36.695
This far in?

11:37.154 --> 11:38.072
Let's take it out!

11:38.197 --> 11:40.658
We can't let it get any further in!

11:57.174 --> 11:59.510
The right wing has been wiped out?

11:59.677 --> 12:02.138
Then why aren't we retreating?

12:02.221 --> 12:03.222
I don't know!

12:03.305 --> 12:04.640
Commander's orders!

12:04.807 --> 12:06.809
Just pass the message on to the left!

12:15.651 --> 12:17.027
What's the deal?

12:17.820 --> 12:20.114
We've been going east for a while now.

12:20.197 --> 12:21.115
FIRST ROW, THIRTEENTH
SCOUT

12:21.198 --> 12:23.951
Yes, and our destination
is the old city to the south.

12:24.660 --> 12:27.621
At this rate, the formation
is going to run right into it!

12:27.997 --> 12:28.831
Yes.

12:29.331 --> 12:30.541
There it is.

12:31.375 --> 12:32.960
A forest of giant trees!

12:39.592 --> 12:41.594
It looks like Titans
have passed through here.

12:44.180 --> 12:46.307
The path is devoid of vegetation.

12:50.728 --> 12:52.146
Even the wagons could get through here.

12:54.064 --> 12:55.483
Inform those behind us

12:56.192 --> 12:59.487
that only the center cart guard team
is to enter the forest.

12:59.862 --> 13:00.696
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

13:15.503 --> 13:16.879
Excuse me, sir.

13:17.338 --> 13:20.216
It looks like the center rank
is entering the forest.

13:20.758 --> 13:23.552
We'll bump into the forest
if we keep going.

13:25.471 --> 13:26.347
Then we go around.

13:27.306 --> 13:28.224
Yes, sir!

13:31.936 --> 13:32.937
Hey, now.

13:33.187 --> 13:35.564
What are we doing
at this tourist attraction?

13:36.148 --> 13:37.650
Now we're really straying

13:37.733 --> 13:40.069
from our original destination
and return point!

13:41.153 --> 13:42.112
I don't know.

13:43.072 --> 13:45.950
I don't know,
but this is what Commander Erwin decided.

13:46.534 --> 13:48.786
He seems to have some kind of plan
in mind, but...

13:49.245 --> 13:51.038
Plan? Are you kidding me?

13:51.747 --> 13:55.626
What? Is he going to throw a welcome party
for us rookies at this tourist spot?

13:56.043 --> 13:58.295
No, I don't think so.

13:58.587 --> 13:59.630
That was a joke.

14:00.464 --> 14:03.634
Either way,
we got that giant broad after us.

14:04.260 --> 14:08.389
Regardless of what plan he has,
we can't afford to stop here.

14:09.139 --> 14:13.394
My guess is we're passing through here
on our way to somewhere else.

14:13.978 --> 14:15.437
All soldiers, halt!

14:19.149 --> 14:21.652
All right! Listen up, rookies!

14:22.278 --> 14:24.446
We're now going to
take up intercept positions!

14:24.780 --> 14:26.615
Unsheathe and wait in the trees!

14:27.199 --> 14:30.703
If any Titans try to enter the forest,
stop them with full force!

14:30.995 --> 14:31.871
What?

14:32.246 --> 14:33.330
Sir?

14:33.539 --> 14:35.749
- Why would we need to--
- Shut up and follow orders!

14:40.588 --> 14:41.755
You've got to be kidding me.

14:42.006 --> 14:43.632
What the hell is happening?

14:47.803 --> 14:49.263
Hey.

14:49.763 --> 14:52.558
It looks like only the center rank went
into the forest.

14:52.766 --> 14:54.226
What does that mean for the formation?

14:54.810 --> 14:56.228
There is no formation anymore.

14:57.229 --> 15:01.692
The forest is blocking us, side squads,
so our only choice is to go around.

15:02.568 --> 15:04.486
We've lost our spotting capabilities.

15:05.779 --> 15:08.407
Why didn't we change course
and avoid the forest altogether?

15:08.991 --> 15:11.744
Did Commander Erwin misread his map
or something?

15:12.411 --> 15:13.370
I don't know.

15:14.079 --> 15:16.457
It's possible we got pushed here,

15:16.957 --> 15:19.126
trying to avoid the threat
on the right side.

15:19.418 --> 15:20.377
Maybe.

15:29.136 --> 15:31.263
This is insane.

15:32.264 --> 15:35.559
First, we abandon our original plan
of establishing a logistics base.

15:36.310 --> 15:39.480
Then instead of running home with
our tails between our legs like we should,

15:40.230 --> 15:42.691
we go on a daring sightseeing tour.

15:43.651 --> 15:45.778
And if that wasn't enough,

15:46.487 --> 15:48.989
now we're just supposed to stand here
and keep Titans out of the forest?

15:52.493 --> 15:56.038
Him and his idiotic orders.

15:56.664 --> 15:57.831
He's going to hear you.

15:58.207 --> 16:01.669
And he doesn't even explain anything.
That's a new one to me.

16:02.002 --> 16:05.923
But I doubt he's that calm
on the inside either.

16:06.340 --> 16:07.257
What do you mean?

16:07.716 --> 16:11.887
Sometimes leaders get deemed incompetent
by their men in extreme situations

16:12.346 --> 16:16.058
and end up dying
from mysterious stab wounds to the back.

16:16.517 --> 16:19.311
It's not that rare. That's all I'm saying.

16:20.270 --> 16:22.815
Jean, what are you thinking of doing?

16:23.691 --> 16:25.192
Relax, will you?

16:25.818 --> 16:28.195
I'm just a little irritated
at this whole situation.

16:29.238 --> 16:33.075
I'm going to follow orders, of course.

16:33.784 --> 16:35.577
Keeping Titans out of the forest?

16:37.496 --> 16:40.708
You agree that's
what we should do too, right?

16:42.376 --> 16:44.294
You look like you know something.

16:44.962 --> 16:46.130
Well...

16:47.881 --> 16:49.508
A 5-meter Titan is approaching!

16:56.306 --> 16:59.601
Why did he bring the platoon here?

17:00.269 --> 17:03.480
Just what is Commander Erwin thinking?

17:04.523 --> 17:05.733
No, that's not right.

17:06.442 --> 17:08.027
That isn't what I should be asking.

17:08.736 --> 17:11.030
What I should be asking is,

17:11.739 --> 17:14.116
what if the Female Titan is pursuing Eren

17:14.742 --> 17:18.078
and the Commander is aware of that?

17:19.538 --> 17:20.456
Captain!

17:20.873 --> 17:22.041
Captain Levi!

17:22.666 --> 17:23.625
What?

17:24.126 --> 17:25.294
"What?"

17:25.377 --> 17:26.712
This is a forest, sir!

17:27.337 --> 17:29.965
We have no way of detecting
the approaching Titans this far in

17:30.215 --> 17:32.051
with only the center rank!

17:32.593 --> 17:34.803
Something seems to be on our right too.

17:35.179 --> 17:39.183
How are we supposed to avoid the Titans
or protect the wagons now?

17:39.475 --> 17:41.977
Quit whining about the obvious.

17:42.519 --> 17:44.605
We can't do any of those things anymore.

17:45.647 --> 17:47.232
But why?

17:47.775 --> 17:49.359
Take a good look around, Eren.

17:49.985 --> 17:51.987
See all these absurdly huge trees?

17:54.490 --> 17:58.077
This is the perfect environment
for using omnidirectional mobility gear.

17:59.369 --> 18:03.624
And use that middling head of yours
to think.

18:04.083 --> 18:06.835
Use your brain for once
if you don't want to die.

18:07.503 --> 18:08.337
Yes, sir!

18:09.755 --> 18:10.756
I see.

18:11.340 --> 18:14.718
I'm still new to this, that's why
I don't understand the situation.

18:15.219 --> 18:17.554
And he won't give me a straight answer

18:17.805 --> 18:19.890
because I still need to learn for myself.

18:20.808 --> 18:24.353
I bet that's how these experts learned
to fight too.

18:26.522 --> 18:29.358
Damn it. What are we doing here?

18:29.650 --> 18:30.984
Seriously.

18:31.235 --> 18:33.654
What the hell is going on?

18:34.947 --> 18:35.823
What?

18:36.281 --> 18:37.282
Don't tell me...

18:38.033 --> 18:43.163
Don't tell me no one knows
what's going on?

18:44.206 --> 18:48.085
Not even Captain Levi?

18:50.045 --> 18:54.758
If my theory is correct
that the Female Titan is after Eren,

18:54.842 --> 18:56.969
then there's only one reason
why we've come here.

18:58.011 --> 19:01.640
Commander Erwin intends
to confront her here!

19:01.932 --> 19:02.766
Armin.

19:03.976 --> 19:08.689
Our order is to keep Titans
out of the forest, right?

19:11.275 --> 19:12.192
In other words,

19:12.734 --> 19:15.737
we don't need to actually fight them.

19:17.030 --> 19:18.073
Right?

19:52.399 --> 19:55.027
- A black smoke signal?
- From right behind us!

19:55.485 --> 19:57.654
It must be whatever is on the right!

19:58.530 --> 19:59.990
Draw your swords.

20:03.452 --> 20:05.454
If it shows itself,

20:06.288 --> 20:07.581
we'll only have a moment.

20:32.064 --> 20:32.898
Move!

20:47.829 --> 20:48.747
It's fast!

20:49.081 --> 20:51.708
There's no way to avoid it
inside this forest!

20:51.792 --> 20:52.960
It's catching up!

20:53.043 --> 20:55.337
Captain! Let's switch
to omnidirectional mobility!

20:55.796 --> 20:56.838
Captain!

20:59.091 --> 21:00.550
You're not going anywhere!

21:01.176 --> 21:02.552
Reinforcements from the rear!

21:18.443 --> 21:20.404
Captain! Give your orders!

21:20.696 --> 21:22.948
Let's take it out! It's dangerous!

21:23.448 --> 21:25.033
We should take care of it!

21:27.035 --> 21:28.578
I'll cut it to shreds!

21:30.789 --> 21:33.709
Idiot! You walked
right into your own doom!

21:34.251 --> 21:37.629
What you're chasing
is a team of expert Titan-killers!

21:40.507 --> 21:41.842
Captain Levi!

21:42.926 --> 21:44.052
Captain!

21:44.344 --> 21:47.472
- Please give us orders!
- It's about to catch up to us!

21:47.931 --> 21:49.182
Let's take it out here!

21:49.266 --> 21:53.270
That's why we entered this forest!
Isn't it, Captain?

21:53.353 --> 21:55.063
Captain! Your orders!

21:58.483 --> 22:00.569
Everyone, cover your ears.

23:43.421 --> 23:47.008
The Female Titan continues to chase them,
leaving a bloodbath behind.

23:47.717 --> 23:52.180
Eren can only flee as he watches
his comrades die before his very eyes.

23:52.889 --> 23:55.684
Amid this, he's forced to make a decision.
